    "indications_en": "Allopurinol is indicated for reducing urate/uric acid formation in conditions where urate/uric acid deposition has already occurred (e.g. gouty arthritis, skin to phi, nephrolithiasis). Allopurinol is indicated for management of 2,8-dihydroxyadenine (2,8-DHA) renal stones related to deficient activity ... Read moreAllopurinol is indicated for reducing urate/uric acid formation in conditions where...",
