    "precautions_bn": "বিশেষ সতর্কবার্তা:\n• চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ অনুযায়ী নিয়মিত সেবন করুন।\n• শিশুদের নাগালের বাইরে নিরাপদ স্থানে সংরক্ষণ করুন।",
    "pregnancy_bn": "গর্ভাবস্থায় ও স্তন্যদানকালে বিশেষ সতর্কতা অবলম্বন করুন। চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ ব্যতীত সেবন নিষেধ।",
    "work_en": "Indicated for Vertigo. Used in clinical management of specialised therapeutics.",
    "primary_indication_en": "Vertigo",
    "indications_en": "Betahistine Mesylate is indicated in vertigo and dizziness associated with the following diseases: Meniere's disease, Meniere's syndrome, Peripheral vertigo.",
    "dosage_en": "Usually, for adults, administer orally 1 to 2 tablets three times per day after meals. The dose may be adjusted according to the age of patient and severity of symptoms.",
    "side_effects_en": "Digestive: Nausea or vomiting may rarely occur. Hypersensitivity: Hypersensitivity reactions, such as skin rash, may rarely occur.",
    "precautions_en": "Patients with a history of digestive ulcer or an active digestive ulcer, Patients with bronchial asthma, Patients with pheochromocytoma.",
    "how_it_works_en": "Betahistine Mesilate dilates precapillary sphincters, increasing the blood flow in the inner ear. It controls the permeability of capillaries in the inner ear, thereby removing endolymphatic hydrops. It also improves cerebral circulation, increasing blood flow in the internal carotid artery. Thus, Betahistine Mesylate is clinically useful for the relief of vertigo and dizziness. Betahistine Mesila...",
    "pregnancy_en": "Safety of Betahistine during pregnancy has not been established. This drug should be administered to pregnant patients or women suspected of being pregnant, only if the expected therapeutic benefit is thought to outweigh any possible risk.",
