    "precautions_en": "Risk of Bleeding: Can cause bleeding. Promptly evaluate any signs or symptoms of blood loss. Spinal/Epidural Anesthesia or Puncture: When neuraxial anesthesia (spinal/epidural anesthesia) or spinal/epidural puncture is employed, patients treated with antithrombotic agents for prevention of thromboembolic complications are at risk of developing an e...",
    "how_it_works_en": "Betrixaban is a factor Xa inhibitor that selectively blocks the active site of factor Xa and does not require a cofactor (such as Anti-thrombin III) for activity. Betrixaban inhibits free factor Xa and prothrombinase activity. By directly inhibiting factor Xa, Betrixaban decreases thrombin generation (TG). Betrixaban has no direct effect on platelet aggregation.",
