    "side_effects_en": "The following clinically significant adverse reactions are described elsewhere in the labeling: • Increased Risk of Thrombotic Events after Premature Discontinuation • Risk of Bleeding • Spinal/Epidural Anesthesia or Puncture • Thromboembolic and Bleeding Events in Patients with Prosthetic Heart Valves • Increased Risk of Thrombosis in Patients wit...",
    "precautions_en": "Bleeding: Dabigatran Etexilate can cause serious and fatal bleeding Bioprosthetic heart valves: Dabigatran Etexilate use not recommended Increased Risk of Thrombosis in Patients with Triple-Positive Antiphospholipid Syndrome: Dabigatran Etexilate use not recommended",
    "how_it_works_en": "Dabigatran and its acyl glucuronides are competitive, direct thrombin inhibitors. Because thrombin (serine protease) enables the conversion of fibrinogen into fibrin during the coagulation cascade, its inhibition prevents the development of a thrombus. Both free and clot-bound thrombin, and thrombin-induced platelet aggregation are inhibited by the active moieties. At recommended therapeutic doses...",
