    "side_effects_en": "The most common side effects are dry mouth & constipation. Other less commonly reported side effects include- abnormal vision, back pain, dry skin, hypertension, vomiting, peripheral edema, weight gain, arthralgia, bronchitis, pharyngitis, rhinitis, sinusitis, rash, pruritus, urinary tract disorder and vaginitis.",
    "precautions_en": "Darifenacin should be used with caution in the patient at risk for urinary retention & decreased gastrointestinal motility, with impaired renal & hepatic impairment.",
    "how_it_works_en": "Darifenacin is a potent, competitive and selective muscarinic receptor antagonist which has greater binding affinity for muscarinic M3 receptors. M3 receptors are involved in the contraction of the detrusor muscle of the bladder, GI smooth muscle, saliva production, and iris sphincter function. Darifenacin may increase volume threshold in patients with involuntary detrusor contraction, thus increa...",
    "pregnancy_en": "Pregnancy Category C. Darifenacin should be used during pregnancy only if the benefit to the mother outweighs the potential risk to the fetus. Lactation: It is not known whether Darifenacin is excreted into human milk and therefore caution should be...",
    "pregnancy_category": "C",
    "brands": "Darifen, Darifen ER, Darifenacin ER, Darilax 15 ER, Darilax 7.5 ER"
