    "precautions_en": "• Prolonged use of corticosteroids may result in glaucoma & posterior subcapsular cataract formation. If this product is used for 10 days or longer, IOP should be monitored. • Use of a corticosteroid medication in the treatment of patients with a history of herpes simplex requires great caution. • Fungal infections of the cornea are particularly pr...",
    "how_it_works_en": "Corticosteroids inhibit the inflammatory response to a variety of inciting agents and may delay or slow healing. They inhibit edema, fibrin deposition, capillary dilation, leukocyte migration, capillary proliferation, fibroblast proliferation, deposition of collagen, and scar formation associated with inflammation. There is no generally accepted explanation for the mechanism of action of ocular co...",
    "pregnancy_en": "Pregnancy Category C. Difluprednate has been shown to be embryotoxic and teratogenic when administered subcutaneously to rabbits. Since use of Difluprednate during human pregnancy has not been evaluated so Difluprednate should be used during pregnanc...",
