    "dosage_en": "Glipizide & Metformin should be given once or twice daily with meals and should be initiated at a low dose, with gradual dose escalation. Glipizide & Metformin as Initial Therapy: The recommended starting dose is 250 mg/2.5 mg once a day with meal. Glipizide & Metformin as Second-Line Therapy: The recommended starting dose is 500 mg/2.5 mg or 500 mg/5 mg twice daily with the morning and evening me...",
    "side_effects_en": "The most common side effects of Glipizide & Metformin are hypoglycemia, diarrhea, nausea/vomiting, abdominal pain, headache, musculoskeletal pain etc.",
    "precautions_en": "Metformin is known to be substantially excreted by the kidney, and the risk of Metformin accumulation and lactic acidosis is increased with the degree of impairment of renal function. Thus, patients with serum creatinine levels above the upper limit of normal should not receive Metformin. In patients with advanced age, Metformin should be carefully...",
    "how_it_works_en": "Metformin is a biguanide antihyperglycemic agent, which improves glucose to lerance in patients with type 2 diabetes, lowering both basal and postprandial plasma glucose. Its pharmacological mechanisms of action are different from other classes of oral antihyperglycemic agents. Metformin decreases hepatic glucose production, decreases intestinal absorption of glucose, and improves insulin sensitiv...",
    "pregnancy_en": "Contraindicated during Pregnancy & Lactation",
