    "how_it_works_en": "Glipizide lowers blood glucose by stimulating the release of insulin from the pancreas, an effect dependent upon functioning beta cells. The extrapancreatic effects of Glipizide are increase in insulin sensitivity and decrease in hepatic glucose production.",
    "pregnancy_en": "Pregnancy: Glipizide should be used during pregnancy only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the foetus. Prolonged severe hypoglycaemia (4-10 days) has been reported in neonates born to mothers who were receiving sulphonylurea (...",
