    "precautions_en": "Ibandronic Acid: • Upper Gastrointestinal Adverse Reactions: Ibandronic acid like other bisphosphonates administered orally may cause local irritation of the upper gastrointestinal mucosa. Because of these possible irritant effects, caution should be used when Ibandronic acid is given to patients with active upper gastrointestinal problems (such as...",
    "how_it_works_en": "Ibandronic Acid (Ibandronate Sodium Monohydrate) is a nitrogen- containing bisphosphonate that inhibits osteoclast-mediated bone resorption. The action of Ibandronate on bone tissue is based on its affinity for hydroxyapatite, which is part of the mineral matrix of bone. Ibandronate inhibits osteoclast activity and reduces bone resorption and turnover. In postmenopausal women, it reduces the eleva...",
    "pregnancy_en": "Pregnancy category C. There are no adequate and well-controlled studies in pregnant women. This kit should be used during pregnancy only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the mother and fetus. Nursing mother: It is not known wh...",
