    "precautions_en": "Hyperlipidaemia: The use of Lorlatinib has been associated with increases in serum cholesterol and triglycerides. Median time of occurrence of severe increase in serum cholesterol and triglycerides is 201 days (range: 42 to 518 days) and 127 days (range: 15 to 358 days), respectively. Serum cholesterol and triglycerides should be monitored before i...",
    "how_it_works_en": "Lorlatinib is a kinase inhibitor with in vitro activity against ALK and ROS1 as well as TYK1, FER, FPS, TRKA, TRKB, TRKC, FAK, FAK2, and ACK. Lorlatinib demonstrated in vitro activity against multiple mutant forms of the ALK enzyme, including some mutations detected in tumors at the time of disease progression on crizotinib and other ALK inhibitors. in mice subcutaneously implanted with tumors har...",
    "pregnancy_en": "Women of childbearing potential/Contraception in males and females: Women of childbearing potential should be advised to avoid becoming pregnant while receiving Lorlatinib. A highly effective non-hormonal method of contraception is required for femal...",
