    "pregnancy_en": "Pregnancy: Magnesium sulfate injection should be used during pregnancy only if clearly needed. Magnesium sulfate is not known to be harmful for short-term intravenous administration in eclampsia but excessive doses cause neonatal respiratory depressi...",
