    "precautions_en": "Treatment with Ramipril and Hydrochlorothiazide combination requires regular medical supervision. Generally dehydration, reduced blood volume (hypovolumia) or salt depletion should be corrected before initiating the treatment (in patients with concomitant heart failure, however, this must be carefully weighed against the risk of volume overload). S...",
    "how_it_works_en": "Ramipril is an angiotensin converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor, which after hydrolysis to ramiprilat, blocks the conversion of angiotensin I to the vasoconstrictor substance, angiotensin II. So, inhibition of ACE by ramipril results in decreased plasma angiotensin II, which leads to decreased vasopressor activity and decreased aldosterone secretion. Thus ramipril exerts its antihypertensive activity...",
    "pregnancy_en": "ACE inhibitors can cause foetal and neonatal morbidity and death when administered to pregnant women. Also, thiazides cross the placental barrier and appear in cord blood. There is a risk of foetal or neonatal jaundice, thrombocytopenia, and possibly...",
