    "precautions_en": "Take special care with if you: • Have low blood calcium (hypocalcemia). • Cannot sit or stand up for 30 minutes. • Have kidneys that work poorly. • Have an allergy to Risedronate Sodium. • Are pregnant or may become pregnant. • Are breast-feeding or plan to breast-feed. • Have kidney problems, Risedronate Sodium may not be right for you.",
    "how_it_works_en": "Risedronate has an affinity for hydroxyapatite crystals in bone and acts as an antiresorptive agent. At the cellular level, Risedronate inhibits osteoclasts. The osteoclasts adhere normally to the bone surface, but show evidence of reduced active resorption. Calcium suppresses parathyroid hormone (PTH) secretion and decreases bone turnover. Increased levels of PTH are known to contribute to age-re...",
