    "how_it_works_en": "Sodium thiosulfate acts as an antidote in the treatment of cyanide poisoning. It acts as a sulphur-donating substrate for the enzyme rhodanese, thus speeding up the conversion of cyanide to thiocyanide, which is relatively non to xic. It is often used in combination with sodium nitrite but may be used alone in less severe poisoning.",
