    "side_effects_en": "The frequency of side-effects is low at the recommended doses. Side-effects which have been recorded such as tremor, headache, to nic cramp and palpitations are all characteristic of sympathomimetic amines. A few patients feel tense; this is also due to the effects on skeletal muscle and not to direct CNS stimulation. Whenever these side-effects ha...",
    "precautions_en": "Care should be taken with patients suffering from myocardial insufficiency or thyrotoxicosis. Due to the hyperglycaemic effects of β2-stimulants, additional blood glucose measurements are initially recommended when Terbutaline therapy is commenced in diabetic patients. If a previously effective dosage regimen no longer gives the same symptomatic re...",
    "how_it_works_en": "Terbutaline is a relatively selective β2-adrenergic bronchodilator that has little or no effect on alpha-adrenergic receptors. The drug has exerts a preferential effect on β2-adrenergic receptors but stimulates beta-adrenergic receptors less selectively than relatively selective β2-agonists. Terbutaline appears to have a greater stimulating effect on beta-receptors of the bronchial, vascular, and...",
    "pregnancy_en": "Although no teratogenic effects have been observed in animals or in patients, Terbutaline should only be administered with caution during the first trimester of pregnancy. Terbutaline is secreted via breast milk, but effect on the infant is unlikely...",
